But it depends on what you are willing to accept as preparation.
If you have never had explored the game using -X mode, never read any
spoilers (or inspected the source files), especially for maps, monsters,
and objects, then you will do much harder than others.

There is a, umm, say game-philosophical view on that...
An adventurer that would enter such a dungeons (in RL), not knowing about
former heros, and not sharing their knowledge, will do much harder and
easily die. (Anybody playing that way?)
In (NH-)practice you will use the experience of previously failing heroes
and avoid critical situations, will know about prices of items, will know
where to go and what to do.
So it makes no difference in principle, apart from reducing the time to
succeed in game, to use the spoilers.

Well, if you have already used the spoilers and -X mode, then I think it
must be the above mentioned patience. Don't play overtired, play when you
are in good mood, don't play more than eight hours a day, don't play less
than five days a week :-)
Retract, write E-word, operate from distance (the darts), pray, survive.

Good luck!

